nightclubs in ireland are to close over  christmas and new year and the  government is to bring back tighter  restrictions for pubs and bars the move  is expected to add to pressure on boris  johnson to consider changing his  position on christmas celebrations in  the uk  it's because of the new omicron covid  variant which is still providing more  questions than answers for scientists  tonight  but new analysis from the uk health  security agency has started to fill in  some of the gaps in our knowledge we'll  have more on that shortly but first here  are the changes announced by the irish  prime minister miguel martin  let's take a look at those new  restrictions nightclubs will be closed  and there'll be strict social distancing  measures put in place in bars and  restaurants a maximum of six adults will  be allowed at a table and there will be  a ban on multiple tables being booked  only three households will be able to  gather in one private dwelling although  mr martin acknowledged there'll be a  need for flexibility  there'll be a maximum of fifty percent  capacity at entertainment cultural and  sporting events and people attending  those must be seated  and covered passes will be extended to  gyms leisure centers hotel bars and  restaurants all restrictions will be in  place from tuesday until the 9th of  january  at every stage of this awful covert  journey  as a country and as a people we have  trusted the science and we have done our  best  we haven't always got it right and there  have been times of great frustration  but  every time we have faced a new challenge  we have pulled together as a nation and  done what was needed  i'm asking all us all to do that again  further study and examination in the  weeks ahead may discover that omicron  does not represent a more deadly threat  and if that is the case it will come as  a great relief to us all  but we simply cannot take that risk with  people's lives and health  this guy's david blevins joins us now  from belfast and david do we know what  exactly has preempted this move  well we had some very sobering words  indeed from the irish prime minister  anti-ship mehol martin in his address to  the nation tonight confirming that there  are two primary causes of concern for  the irish government the unknown level  of threat posed by the new south african  variant even though there has only been  one case of it detected on the island of  ireland ireland so far but also the  potential for a surge in cases as a  result of increased socializing during  the christmas period it's understood the  national public health emergency team  gave the government a very stark warning  earlier that ireland could see up to 15  000 cases of covert after christmas if  it doesn't do something now to curb  social interaction during the festive  period so the government has effectively  turned back the clock to october 22nd by  closing night clubs reimposing  restrictions on their hospitality sector  demanding covert passports for gyms and  leisure centers and  reducing the number of households that  can gather together of course this comes  just a few days after the government  announced that everyone arriving in  ireland would require a negative pcr or  antigen test now you can imagine the  level of devastation there is across the  hospitality industry as we approach  christmas and that happening for the  second year in a row the government's  attempting to reassure them that their  jobs and businesses will be safe by  providing some level of financial  security but let me say this if you're  struck by the contrast between what's  happening in the uk and what's happening  for its closest neighbor do bear in mind  that one part of the uk northern ireland  shares a land border with the republic  of ireland and that creates the bizarre  scenario where you could have a pub in  the republic imposing restrictions in  another one half a mile away effectively  operating as normal
 

